                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "737a115b-213a-32f0-87f0-a8b43bcc1114",
                        "entry_id": "cf8a98b1-85d1-32cd-9053-dc422b95fc81",
                        "glosses": [
                            "iets dat ontstaat door domheid en onnadenkendheid"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ab5eef61-2ce9-4136-97b3-37ba3779ac88",
                                "sense_id": "737a115b-213a-32f0-87f0-a8b43bcc1114",
                                "text": "De zaterdag vóór palmzondag is normaal een dag die veel Denekampers gebruiken om snoeihout aan te voeren. Nu is dat niet mogelijk en wordt er wederom een stukje traditie de das omgedaan. Herman Oude Elferink is uitermate verbolgen over zoveel onnozelheid bij de betrokken bestuurders."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "79e3f69a-8d41-4bbe-a740-0ef34be53d85",
                                "sense_id": "737a115b-213a-32f0-87f0-a8b43bcc1114",
                                "text": "Voor Harry Oude Weernink is de kous inmiddels af, zo schrijft hij aan Eddy Schepers. „Ik ben erg geschrokken en teleurgesteld over de omtrekkende bewegingen en de onnozelheid van uw bestuur inzake deze kwestie, daarom sluit ik van mijn kant de discussie.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "255eed35-b79a-484a-946f-d7299465259a",
                        "source_entry_id": "cf8a98b1-85d1-32cd-9053-dc422b95fc81",
                        "source_sense_id": "737a115b-213a-32f0-87f0-a8b43bcc1114",
                        "target_lang_word": "gullibility",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "gullibility",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ad881a29-5803-3c73-9e4f-ddb7d91915ae",
                                        "entry_id": "3507ff4a-d00f-3318-a833-42b65d7caa05",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quality of readily believing information, truthful or otherwise, usually to an absurd extent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74987f69-8f16-48af-8323-425f4a5f467f",
                                                "sense_id": "ad881a29-5803-3c73-9e4f-ddb7d91915ae",
                                                "text": "What distinguishes the core of the rightwing populist electorate is its gullibility to idiocy-promoting rhetoric against climate science."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "24ef745f-9467-478e-a6d0-5eefef2be83b",
                        "source_entry_id": "cf8a98b1-85d1-32cd-9053-dc422b95fc81",
                        "source_sense_id": "737a115b-213a-32f0-87f0-a8b43bcc1114",
                        "target_lang_word": "silliness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "silliness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "91b16eb8-09a7-3caa-b764-baf1f3a0f6ef",
                                        "entry_id": "09860c26-7af8-3e24-99fe-768fbcdd7b58",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That which is perceived as silly or frivolous."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bfc2ec8c-60e3-4b45-912b-3670d7d92c8c",
                                                "sense_id": "91b16eb8-09a7-3caa-b764-baf1f3a0f6ef",
                                                "text": "The first time Tuvy confided his dream to his mates […] they’d howled with cruel laughter at the outrageousness of it, the silliness of it, the impossibility of it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f6649e53-5149-3f06-8af1-71a56e81832e",
                                        "entry_id": "09860c26-7af8-3e24-99fe-768fbcdd7b58",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An act that is silly; a result of being silly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0433f546-2930-4a75-bd8c-0af49b3639e0",
                        "source_entry_id": "cf8a98b1-85d1-32cd-9053-dc422b95fc81",
                        "source_sense_id": "737a115b-213a-32f0-87f0-a8b43bcc1114",
                        "target_lang_word": "naïveté",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "naïveté",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f9f033b8-bb05-3bb2-948b-ffc5a5a832ba",
                                        "entry_id": "a4eb08ca-adc6-3940-b820-4709fad7f46e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Lack of sophistication, experience, judgement or worldliness; artlessness; gullibility; credulity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d1e0ed4d-de5a-4cce-83df-3241c2c78529",
                                                "sense_id": "f9f033b8-bb05-3bb2-948b-ffc5a5a832ba",
                                                "text": "“You see, I do not know how to pick out any particular part of the diary.” Even while he was speaking an idea dawned upon him, and he said with unconscious simplicity, in a different voice, and with the naïveté of a child: “That’s quite true, upon my honour. Honest Indian!”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "94acffcb-778d-459e-be09-bcb1fe7b6a27",
                                                "sense_id": "f9f033b8-bb05-3bb2-948b-ffc5a5a832ba",
                                                "text": "Maybe Mr. “Buckley” should know to be more skeptical about what’s dished out to him by popular culture. But apart from that, it’s hard to see how it’s his fault. He simply accepted what the most widely available and accessible sources of information claimed was true. For his naïveté, he was systematically misled and bamboozled."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14d53ad0-f03b-426f-a719-f48eecb16a33",
                                                "sense_id": "f9f033b8-bb05-3bb2-948b-ffc5a5a832ba",
                                                "text": "In poring over these vile and well-preserved folders full of antisemitica in the Foreign Ministry archives, one senses a naïveté, even earnestness among Sugihara's generation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
